# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Testing
coverage/
# `*.tgz` is here because this repository's own tooling packs one: `npm pack
# --pack-destination` writes to a temp directory now, but a maintainer running
# `npm pack` by hand -- or a `verify-package.mjs` interrupted between the pack and
# the cleanup -- drops one in the root, where it looks like a release artefact
# and `git add -A` will happily commit it.
*.tgz
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.lcov
.nyc_output/

# Environment variables
#
# `.env` is ignored, and it has to stay ignored: `logging.js` reads a `.env` for
# `ANYDB_*` keys at startup, so a file with a real GCP project id in it is the one
# file in this repository that nobody would think to check before pushing.
#
# `.npmrc` is deliberately NOT ignored, and deliberately not in this list. It is
# committed, it contains one line (`allow-scripts=sqlite3`), and it is the only
# thing that makes this repository's own `npm ci` build the sqlite3 native
# binding on npm 12 -- which blocks install scripts by default. The alternative
# was an `allowScripts` field in `package.json`, which npm reads only for the
# *installing* project and which therefore did nothing for anybody who installed
# this package, while being published to all of them.
#
# `.npmrc.example` is the version for a consumer. It needs no negation: nothing
# above matches it.
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

# Keys and certificates.
# Nothing in this repository is signed, and a `.pem` or `.key` in the index of a
# package that reads database credentials is the worst thing that could happen to
# it. `.npmrc.example` is a real `.npmrc` in spirit, which is why it stays out of
# this list; a real key never is.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore

# IDEs and Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
# Windows is a CI target, so a developer's Explorer window must not become a
# commit.
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Build outputs
dist/
build/

# TypeScript build info, from a contributor who has a `tsc` habit. There is no
# TypeScript here; the file appearing at all means something generated it.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor and patch history
.history/
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~
.#*
\#*#

# Lockfiles other than npm's, in case somebody tries one.
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# scratch
.astfp.cjs
*.code.txt
